;; compiler/native/support.fib: the lIR text of the mailbox protocol and of the call shim (crates/lair/src/capi/{exchange,mailbox,call}.rs). OWNER: package C. STUB: the signatures are final (docs/design/lair-interfaces.md); every function says `todo:`.

;; Fibber cannot export a C function, so the hooks a macro-time module calls and the worker thread are lIR text, compiled once into the process's
;; JIT (docs/design/lair-in-fibber.md 1.5). The text is embedded in the compiler as a string.

(ns native.support)


;; The lIR module of the call shim: a global slot holding callee, argument count and up to eight arguments, and a `void()` function that reads it, switches on the count, calls through the pointer with `ccc` and stores the result. (capi/call.rs `invoke`)
(defun shim-source () -> str
  (trap "todo: native.support shim-source"))

;; The lIR module of the mailbox: worker thread entry (`pthread_create`, 64 MiB stack), a mutex and two condition variables, the hooks of arity 1 and 2, and the state machine of `exchange.rs` with its defined misuse behaviour. (capi/exchange.rs, capi/mailbox.rs)
(defun mailbox-source () -> str
  (trap "todo: native.support mailbox-source"))
